telemetry, not just stub it. Accepted review findings, by id: F-1619b9 (one WARNING per bad shared standard variable; protocol checked once for OTLP) concerns the standard-exporter parsing of tasks 3/4 and is untouched here. F-0ad188 (_Scrubbing keeps _inner; follow _inner until innermost) is task 7.1/4b and untouched. F-fea82d (comma-list exporters, _service_name/_resolve_state/_traces_endpoint signatures) concerns tasks 3/4/6 and is untouched. F-5d64eb (already-set global provider; injected exporter with SDK missing; true+OTEL_SDK_DISABLED+SDK missing; guard shutdown/force_flush raising; span() during shutdown) concerns tasks 4/5/8 and is untouched. F-f4dc92 (bounded-exit thread sets its Event; subprocess must unset MINTMORY_OTEL_ENABLED and patch _endpoint_reachable; otlp_receiver.spans() tuple meaning) concerns tasks 3/5 and 1.2; for the env default this task fixes the value as a literal in the test, so a subprocess test's inherited default is a later task's concern. No # noqa or # type: ignore added.", "criteria": {"C-29c6c2b6": {"tests": ["packages.core.tests.test_telemetry_suite_defaults::test_reset_telemetry_restores_the_noop_shim", "packages.core.tests.test_telemetry_suite_defaults::test_suite_runs_with_otel_disabled_by_default"], "proof": "zero_value", "discriminating": ["packages.core.tests.test_telemetry_suite_defaults::test_reset_telemetry_restores_the_noop_shim", "packages.core.tests.test_telemetry_suite_defaults::test_suite_runs_with_otel_disabled_by_default"]}}, "suppressions": []}
